2,"This Ososo song by Johnson Unuamu Sylvester - FacebookYouTube MusicOsoso language - WikipediaInstagramDocumentation of Ososo language and Ovbiko maiden initiation ...Stream Ososo music | Listen to songs, albums, playlists for ...",https://www.facebook.com/esther.ocheche.2025/videos/this-ososo-song-by-johnson-unuamu-sylvester/854581787033118/,"Nov 12, 2025 · One love to you all. I love this song. This should be our anthem for the year. there own unique voice to it. And sing with. pride and unity for our mother Land. Very impressive and lovely. Esther Ocheche I dey see am ohh…. A beautiful piece. Good to go. C @estherocheche . @estherocheche . @estherocheche . For My Hand (feat. Ed Sheeran) love nwantiti [German Remix] (feat. Joeboy & Kuami Eugene) Infinity (feat. Omah Lay) Tshwala Bam (Remix) (feat. S.N.E) Niger–Congo? Ososo is an Edoid language of Nigeria. The Ososo people are an indigenous community in Edo State, located in Akoko-Edo. They are known for their rich cultural heritage, hospitality, and strong sense of community. Farming is their traditional occupation, and they value hard work, respect for elders, and family unity. The Ososo people celebrate traditional festivals with colorful dances, music, drumming, and cultural displays that ... Mar 8, 2024 · The Ósósọ̀ language (ISO 39-3 oso) is an Edoid language of the Niger-Congo language family. It is spoken by approximately 19,000 people (Ethnologue). There is some slight dialectal variation, but the difference between the Egbetua variety and the Anni/Okhe/Ikpena varieties is largely phonological. Play Ososo and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile.",Ososo,Niger-Congo
